  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Short Explanation:\nProblem:\nSome avatars don't appear in Avatar Menu's preview, then affects every other selected until restart.\nSummary/Replication: \nClick avatar in avatar menu, or have avatar in preview. Only affects some avatars. Theorized to be complex 3.0 avatars.\nRestarting fixes it, until you select the problematic avatar again.\nLong Explanation: \nWhen I click on certain avatars (I think complex 3.0 avatars, I'll explain why I think that further on), the preview doesn't spawn in the Avatar Menu and the avatar performance rank doesn't get updated and becomes unclickable. Clicking on other avatars and changing worlds doesn't fix it. Occasionally, the culprit avatar will spawn at your current coordinates, unparented, falling in place.\nI put \"Break\" in quotations because I still have options to change & Favorite the selected avatar.\nVersion: 2021.5p2\n(Did not occur prior to 2021.5p1) \nFresh Reinstall and removed cache (Whole VRC AppData folder as well), reset profile data, the whole shebang.\nNotes:\nAppears to be a very rare occurrence, my main avatar had this issue, and I don't usually switch my main, so I just got used to it and was waiting for it to be fixed in another update, but noticed no one reported it, at least from what I saw. I said \"complex\" due to it being a 3.0 with a ton of parameters, draw calls, etc. I have another avatar with a different skinned mesh, but same descriptor, and still has this issue. Another avatar, which I did not create, was a 3.0 and had the same problem, but was not as complex as mine. It might not be tied to 3.0 avatars nor it's complexity, but this is what I've been able to gather over the past few days.",
